---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Glimkin: Offline-First RPG Habit Tracker"
  description="Turn daily habits into quests with a 32x32 pixel hero, Gold economy, Streak Shields, and optional Google or GitHub cloud sync."
  activeNav="home"
  includeSchema={true}
>
  <section class="hero-card">
    <div class="hero-header">
      <img
        src="/glimkin-icon.png"
        alt="Glimkin Pixel Hero"
        width="72"
        height="72"
        class="hero-icon"
      />
      <div>
        <span class="badge">OFFLINE-FIRST QUEST TRACKER</span>
        <h1>Glimkin: Turn everyday habits into daily quests.</h1>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      <strong>Glimkin</strong> is a personal offline-first habit tracker app for
      Android and iOS with local SQLite as the single source of truth. Build
      daily streaks, level up a 32x32 pixel hero, earn Gold for gear and Streak
      Shields, and optionally back up your progress across devices. No account
      is required to view this page or use the app offline.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="/privacy" class="btn btn-accent">Read Privacy Policy</a>
      <a href="/terms" class="btn btn-secondary">Terms of Service</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" aria-label="Core features">
    <article class="feature-tile">
      <h2>Local-First &amp; Fast</h2>
      <p>
        Every habit check-in, countdown timer session, and streak update writes
        directly to SQLite on your device. Works completely offline.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-tile">
      <h2>32x32 Pixel Hero &amp; Shop</h2>
      <p>
        Pick Knight, Mage, or Ranger. Earn XP and Gold from completed quests,
        perfect days, streak milestones, and Trophy Case achievements.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-tile">
      <h2>Optional Cloud Sync</h2>
      <p>
        Sign in with Google or GitHub anytime to merge and synchronize your
        habits, logs, settings, and inventory across devices.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>How Glimkin Uses Google Sign-In &amp; Cloud Data</h2>
    <p>
      You can use <strong>Glimkin</strong> completely offline as a guest without
      creating an account. When you voluntarily choose to sign in with Google or
      GitHub for cloud backup, Glimkin requests only basic identity scopes (
      <code>openid</code>, <code>email</code>, and <code>profile</code>) to
      obtain your verified email address and unique provider account ID.
    </p>
    <p>
      Glimkin does not access your Gmail, Drive, Contacts, or Calendar, does not
      generate or process images from Google APIs, and never sells your data.
      Review our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and{" "}
      <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> for full details.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
